# Copy to .env and fill in locally. .env is gitignored and must never be committed.
# Nothing here is required to build the site — the foundation runs with no secrets.

# --- Public (safe to expose)
# LEAVE THIS UNSET for local work. Unset, the site serves its own media from the local
# bucket mirror (media/dist/) and needs no network at all. Set it to the R2 delivery origin
# — with NO trailing slash — to serve from R2 instead. It is the ONLY switch between the
# two, and it is read by both the pages and astro.config.mjs. docs/MEDIA_PIPELINE.md §4.
#
# Not set here on purpose: no delivery hostname exists yet. When one does it will look like
#   PUBLIC_MEDIA_BASE_URL="https://media.nextvisionfilms.com"
# PUBLIC_MEDIA_BASE_URL=""

# --- R2, used by scripts/media-sync.mjs, media-backup.mjs and media-pull.mjs.
# media:pull is READ ONLY and is what a clean checkout (and CI) needs: media/dist/ is
# gitignored and media:build can only reproduce it from the 646 MB of gitignored sources,
# so without the mirror `npm run verify` fails at validate:media. A key with R2 "Object
# Read only" on nvf-media is enough for it; sync and backup need write.
# The site never uses S3 credentials at runtime; it emits plain HTTPS URLs.
# Create at: Cloudflare dashboard -> R2 -> API -> Create API token -> Object Read & Write.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=""
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=""
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=""
# The PUBLIC delivery bucket. Defaults to nvf-media.
R2_BUCKET="nvf-media"
# The PRIVATE source-backup bucket. Never public, never read by the site.
R2_BACKUP_BUCKET="nvf-source-archive"

# --- Cloudflare deploy (CI only; keep these in GitHub Actions secrets, not here)
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=""
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=""

# ============================================================================
# FORMS — the contact endpoint, POST /api/contact/  (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §7)
# ============================================================================
#
# NOTHING HERE IS NEEDED LOCALLY. With all of it unset, `npm run dev` verifies against
# Cloudflare's own always-passes Turnstile TEST secret and delivers to a development sink
# that logs "NOT DELIVERED" and no field contents. `npm run test:forms` drives the whole
# endpoint on a fresh checkout with no account anywhere.
#
# THIS FILE IS NOT WHERE SECRETS GO IN PRODUCTION. A Worker secret is set with
#     wrangler secret put NAME
# and a LOCAL override goes in `.dev.vars` (gitignored, wrangler's own format), never here
# and never in wrangler.jsonc.

# --- Turnstile ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The SITE key is public: it is printed in the HTML of both contact pages, and it is
# worthless without the secret and without the hostname it was issued for. It is read at
# BUILD time, so it is a build variable rather than a Worker secret.
# Unset = Cloudflare's always-passes test key, which is what a local widget renders.
# PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=""
#
# The SECRET is read at REQUEST time from the Worker's environment and never reaches a
# page. Unset in a BUILD, the endpoint refuses every submission with 503 rather than
# accepting one it could not verify.
#   wrangler secret put TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY
#
# Cloudflare's public test values, for `.dev.vars` when exercising the failure paths:
#   always passes  1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
#   always fails   2x0000000000000000000000000000000AA

# --- Delivery ----------------------------------------------------------------
# DECISION D17 IS OPEN: no provider and no recipient have been chosen, and D2 has not
# settled which of three addresses reaches the company. Until they are answered the
# endpoint answers 503 `not-configured` in production and never reports a success.
#
# CONTACT_PROVIDER  "resend" | "brevo" | "dev-sink". Unset = the first adapter whose
#                   credentials are all present, else the dev sink in `astro dev` only.
# CONTACT_RECIPIENT where an accepted message goes.        <- D17 / D2
# CONTACT_SENDER    the From: address. MUST be on a domain the provider has verified.
# CONTACT_PROVIDER=""
# CONTACT_RECIPIENT=""
# CONTACT_SENDER=""
#
# One API key, for whichever provider is chosen. Worker secrets, not build variables.
#   wrangler secret put RESEND_API_KEY      (or BREVO_API_KEY)

# ============================================================================
# ANALYTICS — Cloudflare Web Analytics  (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §8)
# ============================================================================
#
# NOTHING HERE IS NEEDED LOCALLY, and setting it changes nothing in `astro dev`.
# With no token, no analytics script is emitted at all — not a disabled one, not an
# empty tag. A fresh checkout and `npm run test:forms` load zero third-party bytes.
#
# COOKIELESS BY DESIGN. The beacon sets no cookie, writes no localStorage and stores no
# identifier on the device, so no consent banner is required for it. GA4 and Google Ads
# are NOT carried over from the WordPress site; `npm run validate:analytics` fails the
# build if either reappears. Reversing that is decision D19/D8 and would make a consent
# banner mandatory — see docs/BLOCKED_TODOS.md.

# The SITE token, from the Cloudflare dashboard: Web Analytics -> Manage site -> the
# `token` value inside the JS snippet (NOT the whole snippet). Public by definition — it
# is printed in the HTML of every page and authorises nothing. Read at BUILD time.
# BLOCKED: no token exists yet; it needs the owners' Cloudflare account.
# PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_TOKEN=""

# Escape hatch for verifying the integration in `astro dev`. Without it, a token alone is
# not enough to load a beacon outside a production build — a developer's page views are
# not data.
# PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_IN_DEV="true"
